<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 332 0 R
/E (        I turned around, and what I saw was not my friend anymore. His eyes were pitch black, leaking the same liquid that was on the ground. His jaw contorted, stretching all the way to his waist, with circular rows of needle-like teeth. His fingers were three times as long and sharpened into points at the end. Then I saw them, more creatures that looked just like Dmitri, but in lab coats and military uniforms, and behind them all, the creature from my dreams. It was as if it commanded them. It let out a shriek like the sound of glass scratching, and I ran, climbed the ladder, left all my gear except my phone, bolted out of the bunker, and ran out of Chornobyl. I never looked back, knowing my friend was gone, turned into that monster. )
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [1 534 0 R 3]
>>
endobj
