/T (        In sophomore year, back when I consumed horror like Wednesday morning bagels and worshiped Stephen King, I wrote a story about a kid getting eaten by the walls of the school, which turned out to be one sprawling macabre living body itself. I sold it to others as "my toxic relationship with Westtown."          Weirdly enough, the more you try to step away, the more a place swallows you.)
