/Title (It was three in the afternoon, and I had to wake up from the daze cast by the spell of the sun, because nothing was going to alter the fact that I was being propelled forward by time. And so were Other Teacher Ellen and Tiantong.  And so was Westtown. Regardless, the truck filled with the antidote to lethargy and heat and complacency left us with our hands empty save from a few useless words on wilting rectangles. The lemonade dispensers inside the main hall had already been emptied as well.)
